  "verdict": "refutes",
  "confidence": 0.45,
  "method": "analysis.py fetches each Table S1 SBML file from BioModels and integrates it with libroadrunner 2.11.0 (CVODE, absolute and relative tolerance 1e-3, one retry at 1e-8 and 1e-6). An unstimulated run of 1010 time units sets the clamp (100 times the nonzero maximum, or the nonzero minimum divided by 100). Each floating species is then clamped up and down on six pulses of 50, 60, 70, 80, 90 and 100 time units, the stimulus reset every 0.1 time unit, with relaxations between pulses. A directed pair habituates when the first five stimulation-window means are at least 0.001 and each later mean is at most 1/1.5 of the previous. The pre-registered rule is applied to those counts. A second run reproduced the same counts.",
  "results_summary": [
    "30 of 35 Table S1 models were testable. 9 of those 30 had at least one habituating pair, and 6 of 30 had a habituating fraction inside 1% to 50%. Both clauses of the claim fail, so the verdict is refutes.",
    "Across the 30 models there were 4349 scored directed pairs and 23 habituating pairs. Fractions ran from 0.0 to 0.08333333333333333. 21 models had zero habituating pairs. No fraction exceeded 0.50.",
    "Five models were not testable: BIOMD0000000006 has no floating species, BIOMD0000000024 is a delay equation libroadrunner will not load, and BIOMD0000000016, BIOMD0000000483 and BIOMD0000000275 produced no scored pair.",
    "The descriptive flip counter, not used for the verdict, marked 927 pairs and at least one pair in 29 of 30 models. BIOMD0000000203 had none."
  ]
}
